# 02 — Render Pipeline

## 1. Overview

The render pipeline is fully imperative and lives outside React. React owns `<canvas>` and the `Viewport3DRenderModel`. Everything below is Three.js managed by `SceneController`.

```
Viewport3DRenderModel → SceneController → Layer Renderers → <canvas>
```

## 2. Render Model Contract

```typescript
export interface Viewport3DRenderModel {
  domain: DomainRenderModel | null;
  topology: TopologyRenderData | null;
  scalarField: ScalarFieldRenderData | null;
  vectorField: VectorFieldRenderData | null;
  layers: LayerVisibility;
  selection: SelectionRenderData;
  cameraHint: CameraHint | null;
  displayMode: DisplayMode;
  clip: ClipPlaneConfig | null;
  status: ViewportResourceStatus;
}

export type DisplayMode = "shaded" | "wireframe" | "shaded+wireframe" | "flat-shaded" | "points";
```

### Key Sub-Types

- **TopologyRenderData:** `positions: Float32Array`, `indices: Uint32Array | null`, `normals`, `topologyRevision`, `domainKind`
- **ScalarFieldRenderData:** `values: Float32Array`, `min/max`, `quantityId`, `colorMapName`, `fieldRevision`
- **VectorFieldRenderData:** sampled glyph origins, directions, magnitudes, `fieldRevision`
- **LayerVisibility:** boolean flags per layer (meshSurface, wireframe, vectors, scalar, selection, axes, airbox, clip)

## 3. SceneController

One instance per `ViewportPane`. Plain TypeScript class, not React.

- Creates `THREE.WebGLRenderer`, `THREE.Scene`, camera (perspective or orthographic per pane preset)
- Instantiates all layer renderers and registers them
- `render(model)` → updates all layers → `renderer.render(scene, camera)`
- `resize(w, h)` → updates camera aspect + renderer size
- `dispose()` → calls `WebglResourceTracker.releaseAll()`

## 4. Layer Renderers

Each implements `LayerRenderer { update(model): void; dispose(): void; }`. Independent — one layer cannot own another's resources.

| Layer | Rebuild trigger | GPU resources | Key logic |
|---|---|---|---|
| `MeshLayerRenderer` | topology revision | BufferGeometry, Material, Mesh | FEM: triangles; FDM: instanced cubes. No `discretization` fork — topology data is pre-adapted. |
| `FieldSurfaceRenderer` | field revision | vertex color attribute or shader texture | Updates attribute buffer, **not** geometry. Quantity switch ≠ topology rebuild. |
| `VectorGlyphRenderer` | field revision | InstancedMesh with cone geometry | Reuses base glyph; updates instance matrices. |
| `WireframeLayerRenderer` | topology revision | LineSegments or WireframeGeometry | Overlay on shaded mesh. |
| `SelectionLayerRenderer` | selection change | Outline material or separate highlighted mesh | Stencil outline or scaled-normal shell. |
| `AxesGridRenderer` | domain bounds | AxesHelper, GridHelper | Static after load. |
| `AirboxRenderer` | domain bounds | Wireframe BoxGeometry | Static after load. |
| `ClipPlaneRenderer` | clip config | THREE.Plane + cap geometry | Sets clip plane on renderer. |

## 5. Dirty Render Loop

```typescript
type DirtyReason = "camera" | "resize" | "topology" | "field" | "quantity"
  | "layer" | "selection" | "display-mode" | "clip" | "context-restored" | "explicit-animation";
```

- `markDirty(reason)` adds to set + schedules single RAF
- Coalescing: multiple marks in same microtask → one frame
- After render: dirty set cleared, reasons logged to diagnostics
- **Idle = zero frames.** No render without dirty reason.

## 6. WebGL Resource Tracker

Categorized registry (`geometry`, `material`, `texture`, `renderTarget`, `instance`).

- `track(category, resource)` — register
- `releaseCategory(category)` — dispose all in category
- `releaseAll()` — module unmount
- `getCounts()` — diagnostics surface

## 7. Context Loss Recovery

1. `contextlost` → `preventDefault()`, mark resources stale
2. `contextrestored` → `releaseAll()`, rebuild from current model, dirty(`context-restored`)
3. No data refetch — CPU-side buffers still valid in resource hooks

## 8. Display Mode per Pane

| Mode | Material | Wireframe | Lighting |
|---|---|---|---|
| `shaded` | MeshStandardMaterial | no | 3-point + ambient |
| `wireframe` | MeshBasicMaterial(wireframe) | — | none |
| `shaded+wireframe` | MeshStandardMaterial | yes (overlay) | 3-point |
| `flat-shaded` | MeshStandardMaterial(flatShading) | no | ambient |
| `points` | PointsMaterial | no | none |

Mode switch changes material uniforms — **no topology rebuild**.
